4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317066/field-1" "q-317066/field-2" "q-317066/field-3" "q-317066/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317066"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5431"] :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/c3c56ecc3e59befc020d3fb3c636c5831314b05d420dc89fb6d0e1c46a22fd25.png)" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/4e3cee63e90fa235c9b43ca40c4e7dbe854ec75221482000288e3944cf9ce6ad.png)\n    Notice that\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/9bd6fc63a6e7a864954ad754c0467857aec0ab1e288755a286633b657d369072.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/0b8af627003945f3d329d6887260b217ce8d72fea1c8fdd9dcc92c2db26a3992.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5433"] :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/4a4616061123e27093fa73d17de5c81fb68527b83993cba4eec22fc0368fe364.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/c5e95c3c6c86e0719be77fc3db865c7a81995ef386ce7508ccef19ab307a783a.png) Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/e6c0ddd895406c6b79e4c520a7a4002060c917b51a6070f134be8c47dd63de0b.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5434"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/assets/8ddf6015972344b2afaccf34a63e5ae8c478f326a2b227c45499a1be168ce996.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5432"] :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformati